.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Shell link support

@Contents
$ #Shell link support#
   Here, a shell link is a data object that contains information used to
access another object in the shell's namespace. The objects that can be
accessed through shell links are files, folders, disk drivers and printers.
   This FAR plugin module can create shell links to files or folders - that 
is, objects visible through FAR file panels.

   ~Create shell link to an object~@CreateShellLink@

   ~Resolve folder link~@ResolveFolderLink@

   ~Shell link support options~@ShellLinkerCfg@

@CreateShellLink
$ #Create shell link to an object#
 When you creating shell link, you may set these its parameters:

 #Where#                           Path  to  shell link file -  desktop
                                 or another panel folder by default -
                                 and  its name consisting of object
                                 name and .lnk extension

 #Description#                     Shell  link  description  consisting
                                 of  configuration  defined  constant
                                 part and object name

     Default  values  of these fields are defined in  dialog
~Shell link support options~@ShellLinkerCfg@
     When  group of shortcuts is created, field {Where} must contain
path only and field {Description} must contain constant part only.
     Press  #Create# button when you agree with values entered,  and
shell link will be created in {Where} placeholder.
     If  link file supposed to be created on desktop by default, you
can create it in another panel folder by pressing #On panel# button.
Vice  versa,  pressing #On desktop# button changes destination  path
from another panel folder to desktop one.
     You  can  change link file name case by pressing #Case# button.
The order is "File name.Ext" -> "File Name.Ext" -> "FILE NAME.EXT" -
> "file name.ext", one step by time.

@ResolveFolderLink
$ #Resolve folder link#
     Shell link support plugin allows to change current panel folder
to  linked one by pressing #Enter# key on shell link file,  if  it's
not a link to another type object.
     This  feature can be turned off , if you wish, in dialog
~Shell link support options~@ShellLinkerCfg@ dialog

@ShellLinkerCfg
$ #Shell link support options#
 In this dialog you can set these parameters:

 #Resolve folder links#            This   checkbox   defines,   is   it
                                 possible  to  change  current  panel
                                 folder  to  linked one  by  pressing
                                 #Enter# on shell link file or not

 #Folder link mask#                File  mask  or set of masks  divided
                                 by   commas.  Plugin  considers  any
                                 file  matched  as a  shell  link  to
                                 folder  and,  therefore,  tries   to
                                 resolve it.

 #Description prefix#              This  text  is  a constant  part  of
                                 description  of newly created  shell
                                 link

 #Create shell links by default:#  This buttons define default path  to
                                 newly created shell link file:

 #On panel#                        in another panel current folder

 #On desktop#                      in desktop folder

